{"Title":"An Act relative to excess profits resulting from 40B developments","BillNumber":"H1356","DocketNumber":"HD373","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"L_M1","Name":"Lenny Mirra","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/L_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T14:35:26.62"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"L_M1","Name":"Lenny Mirra","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/L_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T14:35:26.62"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1356/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Mirra of Georgetown, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1356) of Lenny Mirra relative to the penalty for withholding low income housing development excess profits.  Housing.","DocumentText":"\t Section 21 of chapter 40B of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the first paragraph the following paragraph:-\r\n\t\"Any public agency or limited dividend or nonprofit organization convicted of fraudulently withholding from a city or town of the Commonwealth excess profits from a development under this chapter shall be ineligible to construct any additional developments under this chapter or chapter 40R for a period of 5 years from the date of the conviction.\"\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J28","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J28"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}